{"order":1,"parent_path":[],"source":"`Step.concept_ids` is authoritative and already survives merge and re-ground, but accounting is incomplete across the full lifecycle. `check_concept_coverage()` currently treats an approved `wont_do` node as covered without a structured non-delivery record; split and merge can leave structured deferrals pointing to removed or renumbered steps; and split tests do not directly reject invented IDs or prove exact dry-run ownership distribution.

Re-ground and scope-out render concept IDs into seeds, but create does not consume them as authoritative restoration metadata or reconcile them with the signed concept record. This permits dropped, invented, stale, contradictory, or ambiguously mapped accounting information to escape explicit review. Generated CLI documentation also derives from parser help, so editing the generated README/index directly causes drift-check failures.

The missing invariant is a conservation law covering both delivery and deliberate non-delivery. The evidence to close is `step5-run-reconcile-69028ee5`, `step5-run-reconcile-6b8b7ab0`, `step6-run-reconcile-cb54717a`, `step6-run-reconcile-be1832fa`, `structural-deferral-links`, `forward-seed-ownership-restoration`, and `step10-run-reconcile-d05fb53f`.","title":"problem statement"}
